INT. COUNTY PAROLE OFFICE - NIGHT

Fluorescent light. The kind that hums. A corridor of closed doors and one open one at the end where a lamp burns yellow.

Rain on the window. Rain on the roof. The building ticks as it cools.

He sits alone in the chair across from the empty desk. Waiting. His coat is still damp and he has not taken it off. His hands rest on his knees like something set down and forgotten. Nobody told him the office closed at five. Nobody told him anything.

Silence.

The wall clock says 9:41. The wall clock has said 9:41 since he walked in.

A door opens down the hall. Footsteps, slow, and the squeak of rubber on linoleum. A woman in a long dark cardigan, grey hair pinned back, appears in the doorway with a mug in both hands. She does not look surprised to see him. She looks like she has been expecting him for years.

THE WOMAN
You're late Kip.

KIP
I'm not Kip. I'm Kim.

THE WOMAN
Kim then.

She sits behind the desk. Opens the folder. The folder is very thin.

Nothing.

Her eyes move down the page and then up, and for a moment he thinks he sees something move behind her, a shape in the dark of the hallway, tall, patient.

KIM
Who else is here.

THE WOMAN
Nobody. Just us.

KIM
I heard someone.

THE WOMAN
You hear a lot of things, Kim. It's in your file.

She turns the folder around so he can read. His name. His date of birth. A line of handwriting beneath, in red, that he cannot make himself read aloud.

Rain.

KIM
That's not my handwriting.

THE WOMAN
No. It's his.

KIM
Whose?

She does not answer. The lamp flickers. In the corridor, the footsteps start again, closer now, unhurried.

KIM (CONT'D)
(barely)
Please tell me that's you.

THE WOMAN
I'm right here.

The footsteps stop at the door. He does not turn around. He cannot. Every muscle in his neck has locked.

The Woman closes the folder gently.

THE WOMAN (CONT'D)
My name is Margaret. And that is Kip.

Behind him, the door opens.

Nothing.

Then a breath that is not his own.

KIM
(whispering)
Kip is dead.

MARGARET
Yes.

Silence.

The clock moves. 9:42.
